# Intent: The test hook that lets the private path be proven at home (old patch 153, rebuilt for this tree's single hub link). self.network.prefer_tailnet(minutes) (1 to 60; 0 turns it off) makes the hub link use the private route for that long even though the home address works, and reopens an open link through it (the reconnect loop closes its socket within 5 s of the request). Refused with tailnet_not_ready while the client is not connected and with no_hub_address while no hub private address is saved. Never saved: a restart clears it. It is an MCP tool, so only the authenticated hub connection can call it. The rule is plain C (mt_prefer_* in maipai_tailnet_core.h), tested on the host. self.tailnet.status gains prefer. Cost: 16 bytes of internal RAM, no task.
# Placement: unit (the hub link is the unit's own)
# Upstream: bot patch 153 (prefer-tailnet-hook) of the old firmware, rebuilt; firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc of the Xiaozhi component (MIT)
# Check after a flash: needs a real join. self.network.prefer_tailnet(5) answers {"ok":true,"minutes":5}; the log says 'Private network preference changed: reconnecting to the hub' then 'connecting to the hub over the private network'; the hub sees the unit from a 100.64.0.0/10 address; after five minutes the next reconnect uses the home address again. With the client not connected it answers tailnet_not_ready.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_TAILNET (off removes the hook's loop check).

